\b Middletons POS — Simple User Guide\b0\par
\par
This guide is written for beginners and seniors. Each step tells you exactly what to click and what to type. If something doesn’t work, don’t worry — read the tips at the end or ask a helper.\par
\par
\b Getting Started\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Open the app. A small splash screen shows first; the main window opens automatically.\par
\bullet\tab Along the top are buttons to move around: POS, Receipts, Reports, and Configuration.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Make a Sale (POS)\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Pick Cashier: click “Cashier” and choose your name.\par
\bullet\tab Pick Payment: click “Payment” and choose Cash, Card, Check, or Gift Card.\par
\bullet\tab Add an Item:\par
{\pard\li720
\bullet\tab Item: type what it is (for example “Lamp”).\par
\bullet\tab Price: type the selling price (for example 25 or 25.00).\par
\bullet\tab Vendor: type the vendor’s name or code. Suggestions appear as you type. Press Tab or Enter to accept.\par
\bullet\tab Discount (only if needed): change “Discount” from “No discount” to “Percent” or “Amount,” then type the value (e.g., 10% or $5.00). You can add a reason (optional).\par
\bullet\tab Click “Add Item.”\par
\pard}
\bullet\tab Fix a Mistake: next to any item, click “Edit” (to change it) or “Remove” (to delete it).\par
\bullet\tab Totals: Subtotal, Tax, and Total update automatically. Tax rate shows next to the “Tax” line.\par
\bullet\tab Cash Change: if paying by Cash, a “Cash Received” box appears. Type how much the customer gives you; “Change Due” shows the correct change.\par
\bullet\tab Print & Save: click “Print & Save.” You’ll hear a cash register “ka‑ching.” If Cash, a large message shows the “Change Due.” Click “OK.” Then the receipt print window opens — use your normal print button. After printing, the cart clears for the next sale.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Receipts\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Go to “Receipts” to search past sales.\par
\bullet\tab Filter: Use the search box (receipt #, item, vendor, cashier, or payment). Set From/To dates. Choose Cashier/Payment or leave “All.” Click “Apply.” Use “Clear Filters” to reset.\par
\bullet\tab View/Print: In “Actions,” click “View” to open a receipt or “Print” to print it again.\par
\bullet\tab Void a Receipt (use with care): Click “Void,” choose your name, type a reason (e.g., “duplicate sale”), and confirm. Voided receipts remain listed with a note.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Reports\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Go to “Reports” to see Sales per Vendor and a Credit Card Fee summary.\par
\bullet\tab Dates: Pick “From” and “To,” then click “Run Report.” Shortcuts: “Today” and “Current Month.”\par
\bullet\tab Results: Table shows totals per vendor (cash, card, check, gift card, other), gross total, and item count. The fee section shows 5% of gross card sales per vendor (reference only).\par
\bullet\tab Print: Click “Print” for the summary or “Print Detailed” for per‑vendor details.\par
\bullet\tab Export: Click “Export CSV” to download a spreadsheet of what you see.\par
\bullet\tab Back Up Data (Manual): Click “Backup Data.” Choose a folder and filename (for example, Documents\\Middletons\\Backups). It saves a single .json file with everything.\par
\bullet\tab Restore from Backup (careful): Click “Restore Data,” pick a previous backup file, and confirm. This replaces your current data with the backup.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Automatic Backups\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab When you close the app, it automatically writes “middletons-backup-latest.json” into the app data backup folder (for example, %APPDATA%\\Middletons\\backups).\par
\bullet\tab Automatic backups stay in that app data folder so you can keep manual exports elsewhere; ask a helper if you need the path.\par
\bullet\tab Tip: Do a manual backup once to set your preferred folder.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Vendors\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Go to Configuration → Manage Vendors.\par
\bullet\tab Add a vendor name and an optional short code (like “JSM”). Codes help fast entry on the POS page and show on receipts.\par
\bullet\tab You can edit or delete vendors later.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Cashiers\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Go to Configuration → Manage Cashiers.\par
\bullet\tab Add each cashier’s name so you can select it on the POS screen.\par
\bullet\tab You can edit or remove names later.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Settings\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Go to Configuration → Settings.\par
\bullet\tab Tax Rate: type a decimal (for example 0.0725 for 7.25%) and save. The POS updates tax automatically.\par
\bullet\tab Developer Mode: ignore this unless a helper asks you to turn it on (it exposes a technical “Reindex IDs” tool on the Receipts page).\par
\pard}
\par
\b Everyday Tips\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab If you try to leave the POS page with items in the cart, the app asks you to confirm so you don’t lose a sale by accident.\par
\bullet\tab If the app asks you to select a cashier or payment, pick them at the top of the POS page and try again.\par
\bullet\tab For vendor entry on POS: type the code or name; suggestions appear; press Tab or Enter to fill in the best match.\par
\bullet\tab Keep prices simple: you can type “25” instead of “25.00” — the app formats it.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Good Habits\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Make a manual backup to an easy-to-find folder (like Documents\\Middletons\\Backups); manual copies stay there while automatic backups remain in %APPDATA%\\Middletons\\backups.\par
\bullet\tab Print test: once per day, try printing a test page to ensure the printer is ready.\par
\bullet\tab If something looks wrong, don’t panic: you can void a receipt and re‑ring the sale.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Need Help?\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Ask your support person to help you find your backup folder, printer settings, or to recover from a backup.\par
\bullet\tab If you see a confusing message, write it down (or take a picture) and share it with your helper.\par
\pard}
}
